// ---- Batch 4 (Dhaka division, 2025-2026): machine-transcribed
// from reader JSON (11998 rows -> 11992 entries, 54222 class-rates,
// verified 0-mismatch against reader data). 104 office entries cover
// 104 checklist offices; 3 checklist offices are BLOCKED (no entry):
// Dhaka Sadar (site serves a Munshiganj Sadar document, proven twice),
// Kalukhali (site serves the Pangsha document, proven twice),
// Kishoreganj Sadar (only a 2024-2025 book offered, proven twice).
// - SONARGAON FILTER: the Narayanganj file N=71 is the 322-row Sonargaon
//   book, not a Baidyer Bazar book. ONLY its 31-row Baidyer Bazar
//   section (1-based rows 156-186) merged under baidyer-bazar; the
//   other 291 rows (2025 class-rates) are NOT merged anywhere.
//   Sonargaon itself is NOT a checklist office.
// - DHAKA CITY x100: Uttara, Khilgaon, Sutrapur, Tejgaon, Gulshan,
//   Badda, Dhanmondi, Mohammadpur print per-ayutangsha; values are
//   stored x100 as per-shatangsho. Proofs verified numerically:
//   Gulshan x100 == Pallabi 14/14; Sutrapur x100 == Demra 9/10 claimed
//   (2 cells off by 4000, not adjudicated, each office keeps its own
//   values); Uttara shares Gulshan's scale as-printed. All other
//   offices are per-shatangsho as printed (Nawabganj/Kalampur per-shatak).
// - COLLISION RULES (batch-3 order + Dhaka poura test): distinct thana
//   -> variants[]; distinct JL -> '(JL <jl>)' suffix; exactly-2-rows
//   one-poura -> ' (পৌর)' suffix on the poura row (poura-ness from
//   the row's OWN section label; counterpart references like 'also
//   appears in X পৌরসভা section' do NOT count); own-kromik ->
//   '(ক্রম <n>)'; distinct union/section -> variants[] by union
//   (city rows: thana 'গাজীপুর সিটি কর্পোরেশন'; union == mouza name
//   keeps the full 'ইউনিয়ন <name>' label).
// - MIRZAPUR (Tangail): 8 exact-duplicate re-prints deduped (219 -> 211
//   rows, 19 class-rates); সরিষাদাইড় JL 145/146 kept as two JL-suffixed
//   entries (JL typo not adjudicated).
// - GROUP COLUMNS (batch precedent: one printed value for both classes):
//   Kalampur বাড়ী/ভিটা + ডোবা/পুকুর (parent-ruled, flagged);
//   Nawabganj, Dohar, Keraniganj, Narsingdi Sadar, Nagarpur, Kalihati
//   and other group columns as transcribed by the readers.
// - JOINT CLASSES stay reference-only (never entered): Gachbaria-style
//   fused names — Sripur ভিটাবাড়ী (বাড়ী/ভিটা no_rate, flagged: if
//   ruled a group column, its values need a re-read, they were not
//   transcribed); Hossainpur বাগান বাড়ী; pure দোকান/চান্দিনা/বাসা
//   never বাণিজ্যিক. Combined columns NAMING বাণিজ্যিক explicitly
//   (দোকান/বাণিজ্যিক, বাণিজ্যিক/দোকান) ARE entered per the Nangalkot
//   precedent; Araihazar's 'চান্দিনা ভিটি ও বাণিজ্যিক ভূমি' is the
//   flagged exception (reader treated it ref-only AND did not
//   transcribe its values, so বাণিজ্যিক stays no_rate there pending
//   a value re-read + Pankaj's ruling).
// - UNREADABLE (never guessed): Gazipur 2nd Joint 22 cells (p2 rows
//   18-28 ডোবা+পুকুর) + Hossainpur 2 name cells (values legible,
//   kept under '[নাম অপঠনীয় — ক্রম ১৬/৫২]' placeholders).
// - DECIMALS kept exact (Barangaol Shibloya 8 paisa values, e.g.
